  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:model-capacity",
  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "The measure of a machine learning model's ability to represent a wide variety of functions, determined by parameter count, architecture depth and width, and representational power. Models with insufficient capacity underfit the data; those with excessive capacity risk overfitting. Capacity is formally bounded by concepts such as the Vapnik\u2013Chervonenkis dimension, and is managed in practice through regularisation, pruning, and architecture search.",
